        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Court Cases: Miller v. California; Gates v. Collier\n- Organizations: United States Supreme Court; United States Court of Appeals for the Fifth Circuit\n- Concepts: Obscenity\n\nFacts:\n- In 1973, Miller v. California, 413 U.S. 15, became a landmark decision of the United States Supreme Court.\n- In 1973, the United States Supreme Court in Miller v. California redefined obscenity from material that is “utterly without socially redeeming value” to material that lacks serious literary, artistic, political, or scientific value.\n- Gates v. Collier is reported at 501 F.2d 1291 in the United States Court of Appeals for the Fifth Circuit.",
